        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): add licenses settings screen",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid users did not have an in-app place to inspect bundled third-party/open-source license notices from Settings, and maintainers did not have scoped Android agent guidance for keeping that surface current when dependencies change.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a Settings-tab Licenses section backed by packaged UTF-8 `.txt` assets. The screen discovers license files at runtime, derives row titles from filenames, sorts rows alphabetically, renders individual license bodies as monospace text without extra project headings, and documents the Android maintenance guidance in `apps/android/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users can open Settings, tap Licenses, and read bundled third-party license notices without leaving the app. Maintainers can add or update license notice files on disk without hardcoding new rows in application source.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `./gradlew :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.AndroidLicenseNoticesTest --console=plain`\n- `./gradlew :app:assemblePlayDebug --console=plain`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Live emulator screenshot proof generated locally under `.artifacts/android-license-three-screens-fresh/`:\n  - `01-settings-licenses-row.png`\n  - `02-licenses-list.png`\n  - `03-license-detail-manrope-no-heading.png`\n- Additional artifact summary: `.artifacts/android-license-three-screens-fresh/summary.txt`\n",
